## The 3ct Grade Floor — What GIA Says at 9.4mm

At 3ct, every grade decision is amplified. The stone is 2.1× the face-up area of a [1ct round](/mens-1-carat-diamond-ring). Inclusions that hide at 1ct are obvious at 3ct. Color that reads neutral at 2ct reads warm at 3ct.

**Color:** G is still the floor. At 9.4mm face-up, H reads warm in [white gold](/mens-white-gold-diamond-ring) — more noticeably than at 2ct. G is correct in [yellow gold](/mens-yellow-gold-diamond-ring), white gold, or platinum. F and E add $6,000–$20,000 for a color return you will not see in a men's setting. G is the right call.

**Clarity:** VS2 minimum. At 9.4mm face-up, the inclusions of an SI1 stone are visible in certain lights. VS2 is not negotiable at 3ct. VS1 and VVS grades are for investors or collectors who want the cert to hold premium value.

**Cut:** Excellent only. At 9.4mm, a Very Good cut shows dead zones. The stone goes dark in patches. An Excellent cut throws fire across a room. The difference is not subtle.

| Grade | Natural 3ct Round | What this means |
|---|---|---|
| G-VVS1 | [$44,500](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/29113860?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) | Lowest-priced entry in certified inventory. Eye-clean, colorless. |
| G-VS2 | [$48,780](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/24964101?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) | $4,280 more than G-VVS1. Same color. Slightly lower clarity tier. |
| G-VS1 | [$54,640](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/27540948?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) | $10,140 over entry. One clarity step. Skip for a men's setting. |
| E-VS2 | [$60,880](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/28416523?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) | $16,380 premium for color you will not see. Avoid. |
| F-VS1 | [$65,650](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/29207723?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) | $21,150 over G-VVS1 for color and clarity no one sees in a men's setting. |
| D-VS2 | [$72,930](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/25308687?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) | $28,430 premium. D at 3ct in a men's setting is pure cert buying. |

**Verdict:** G-VVS1 at $44,500 is the entry. G-VS2 at $48,780 is the alternative if you prefer the VS2 tier. Everything above costs $10,000–$28,000 more for a visual return you will not see on a hand.

