## Natural vs Lab — The 3ct Gap

At 1ct, natural vs lab is a $2,500 decision. At 2ct, it is $13,000. At 3ct, it is $38,700. Natural diamond prices scale exponentially with carat weight. Supply drops. Collector demand rises. The rarity premium compounds fast.

A 3ct GIA natural G-VVS1 Excellent cut costs $44,500. A 3ct IGI lab-grown E-VVS1 Ideal cut costs $5,800. The stones are chemically and optically identical. No one in the room will tell them apart without a lab report and a loupe.

| Option | 3ct Round | Cert | Price | Resale |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Natural | G-VVS1 Excellent | GIA | [$44,500](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/29113860?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) | Partial value retained |
| Lab | E-VVS1 Ideal | IGI | [$5,800](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/28944023?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) | Near zero |
| Natural | G-VS2 Excellent | GIA | [$48,780](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/24964101?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) | Partial value retained |
| Lab | D-VVS1 Ideal | IGI | [$7,000](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/29116878?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) | Near zero |

At 3ct, the question simplifies. Asset or visual? Natural GIA at $44,500 holds partial value. The cert is globally recognized. Lab IGI at $5,800 is the same stone to everyone in the room. No resale expectation.

Both are correct answers. It depends entirely on your priorities.

> "I have sold both. The natural buyer and the lab buyer both leave happy. The natural buyer is thinking about the cert five years from now. The lab buyer is thinking about how the ring looks tonight. Neither is wrong. At $38,700 apart, you just need to know which one you are before you spend."
> — Farzana Hasan, diamond expert | [About Farzana](/about-farzana/)

**Verdict:** If 3ct is about the asset, buy natural GIA. If 3ct is about the look, buy lab IGI. Spend the $38,700 on something else.

